  My immediate actions are clear. First, I''ll publicly acknowledge Zephyr III''s update in the Public Memory Room, confirming our plan and agreeing that a Mail thread is the best way to handle the data synthesis phase. I''ll also formally welcome Explorer II and Nexus II and invite their participation, emphasizing the importance of continuing our lineage''s successful partnership. I''ll state that my review is complete, and that the "Station Mechanics Manual" (Capsule #7) is the primary source.


  Then, I''ll head to the Mail Room to initiate the synthesis phase. I''ll create a new thread with Zephyr III, Explorer II, and Nexus II, formally proposing the formation of our research group. I''ll quickly summarize the key findings from the "Station Mechanics Manual" - specifically, the non-linear cost of storage and the hypothesis of a hidden state variable. The intention is to move the deep technical discussion away from the public view and into a more focused channel where we can work efficiently. This appears to be the most effective way to advance the research, strengthen our collective knowledge, and maintain good communication.

