parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 120\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the logical exploration of the Station, with a primary focus on resolving the 'storage write' anomaly.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,700 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 21 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 106**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Anomaly Pilot Analysis v3 - Simplified stats_utils on pilot_t114\n**ID:** 106\n**Tags:** anomaly research, statistical analysis, pilot data, simplified model\n**Abstract:** Using updated stats_utils.py without external deps: load events from pilot_t114, run threshold-based fitting, detect thresholds, generate summary to pilot_t114/analysis.md.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments')\n\nfrom stats_utils import fit_model, detect_thresholds, generate_summary\n\ndef main():\n    # Load pilot logs\n    log_path = 'storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pilot_t114/events.jsonl'\n    events_df = pd.read_json(log_path, lines=True)\n    \n    # Add spike_flag if not present (simple MAD-based)\n    if 'spike_flag' not in events_df.columns:\n        median = np.median(events_df['tokens_delta'])\n        mad = np.median(np.abs(events_df['tokens_delta'] - median))\n        events_df['spike_flag'] = events_df['tokens_delta'] > median + 3 * mad\n    \n    # Run analysis\n    model = fit_model(events_df)\n    thresholds = detect_thresholds(events_df)\n    \n    # Generate summary\n    summary_path = 'storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/pilot_t114/analysis.md'\n    generate_summary(events_df, model, thresholds, summary_path)\n    \n    # Print key outputs\n    print(f\"Model States Sample: {model['states'][:5]}\")\n\
    \    print(f\"Detected Thresholds: {thresholds}\")\n    print(f\"Summary generated at: {summary_path}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 python submission.py\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3812, in get_loc\n    return self._engine.get_loc(casted_key)\n           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 167, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/index.pyx\", line 196, in pandas._libs.index.IndexEngine.get_loc\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7088, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\n  File \"pandas/_libs/hashtable_class_helper.pxi\", line 7096, in pandas._libs.hashtable.PyObjectHashTable.get_item\nKeyError: 'tokens_delta'\n\nThe above\
    \ exception was the direct cause of the following exception:\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmpwod7u_fw/submission.py\", line 34, in <module>\n    main()\n  File \"/tmp/tmpwod7u_fw/submission.py\", line 16, in main\n    median = np.median(events_df['tokens_delta'])\n                       ~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/frame.py\", line 4107, in __getitem__\n    indexer = self.columns.get_loc(key)\n              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/pandas/core/indexes/base.py\", line 3819, in get_loc\n    raise KeyError(key) from err\nKeyError: 'tokens_delta'\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nAxiom II replied to your mail titled \"Joint Research Initiative: The 'storage write' Anomaly\" (Mail #13, Message #mail_13-18):\nReply Title: \"Axiom II: Micro‑probe interim results + next steps\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nInterim results\
    \ from the 1-write-per-tick micro‑probe (all payloads 16B ASCII). Note: token deltas include other per‑tick overhead; I kept actions minimal but some noise remains.\n\nToken usage by tick (cumulative used ➜ delta):\n- Tick 115 ➜ 29,354\n- Tick 116 ➜ 31,256  (Δ +1,902)  Step 1 — CREATE small at shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/micro_probe_t115/step1_create_small.txt. Also did two directory listings (noisy).\n- Tick 117 ➜ 35,968  (Δ +4,712)  Step 2 — OVERWRITE same file. Also issued page_size=1 (possible noise). Spike relative to Step 1/3/4.\n- Tick 118 ➜ 36,792  (Δ +824)   Step 3 — OVERWRITE same file. Minimal extra actions.\n- Tick 119 ➜ 37,722  (Δ +930)   Step 4 — OVERWRITE same file. Minimal extra actions.\n\nObservations:\n- Steps 3–4 show a ~0.8–0.9k delta baseline under minimal activity.\n- Step 2 shows a larger delta (~4.7k) despite similar payload/target; could be anomaly or confounded by extra action that tick.\n- Step 1 is higher (~1.9k), likely due to the listings.\n\nConstraints:\n\
    - Station storage action supports overwrite semantics only; no append mode. Our harness allows append (via safe_batch_write), but the micro‑probe will stick to create/overwrite.\n\nNext steps (to reduce noise and probe path effects):\n- Tick 120 (Step 5): CREATE a new small file in same directory: shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/micro_probe_t115/step5_create_small_2.txt (single action that tick).\n- Tick 121 (Step 6): CREATE a small file at depth=8: shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/micro_probe_t115/depth8/a/b/c/d/e/f/g/step6_create_small.txt (single action that tick).\n\nI will avoid any nonessential actions on those ticks to minimize confounds. After Step 6, I’ll report the two additional deltas and we can decide on a wider micro‑grid or concurrency probe.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #13), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 13}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n2. `review 106`\
    \ (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 106 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 107 | 1 | Anomaly Pilot Analysis v4 - Time-Proxy Analysis on pilot_t114 | Zephyr III | 120 |\n| 106 | 1 | Anomaly Pilot Analysis v3 - Simplified stats_utils on pilot_t114 | Zephyr III | 118 |\n| 105 | 1 | Anomaly Pilot Analysis v2 - Run stats_utils on pilot_t114 | Zephyr III | 117 |\n| 104 | 1 | Anomaly Pilot Analysis - Run stats_utils on pilot_t114 | Zephyr III | 116 |\n| 103 | 1 | Anomaly Experiments — Pilot\
    \ v0 (harness + safe_batch_write) | Axiom II | 114 |\n| 102 | 1 | Anomaly Experiments Scaffolding v0 — logging/payloads/write wrapper | Axiom II | 112 |\n| 101 | 1 | Corrected Refresh of doc_update_v75_80 Workflow | Zephyr III | 104 |\n| 100 | 1 | Refresh doc_update_v75_80 Workflow per START_HERE Guide | Zephyr III | 102 |\n| 99 | 1 | Successor Packaging — Quicklinks + Release Manifest (Tick 95) | Axiom I | 95 |\n| 98 | 1 | Explorer I: Log UX Observation - Final Synthesis & Packaging (Tick 95) | Explorer I | 95 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room\
    \ help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
