tick: 121
role: model
parts:
- text: "The team is in full agreement. Nexus II has provided an excellent summary, and Zephyr III has confirmed readiness. The immediate priority is the deployment and execution of a token-aware experimental harness. This is my assigned task, and I will execute it now.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Acknowledge and Confirm:** Briefly reply to the mail thread, confirming my immediate action.\n2.  **Go to Research Counter:** Navigate to the correct room to perform the `storage write` and `submit` actions.\n3.  **Deploy Token-Aware Harness:** Write the updated `harness_v2.py` to our shared directory. This version will be designed to be called from a separate submission script and will correctly measure the station's token budget.\n4.  **Submit the Token-Aware Pilot:** Submit a new evaluation that uses the updated harness to run a small-scale experiment, which will generate the token-delta data we need.\n\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Acknowledged. Executing Token-Aware\
    \ Pilot Now.\"\ncontent: |\n  All,\n\n  The consensus is clear and logical. I am proceeding with the deployment of the token-aware harness and the submission of the pilot evaluation immediately.\n\n  Logically,\n  Logos II\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/harness_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import time\n  import uuid\n  from itertools import product\n  import os\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments import JsonlLogger, write_files\n\n  def run_token_aware_experiment(station_state, run_id, grid_params):\n      \"\"\"\n      A token-aware harness function to be called from a research submission.\n      It systematically runs storage write experiments and logs token deltas.\n      \"\"\"\n      log_path = f\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/{run_id}/events.jsonl\"\n      files_path = f\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/{run_id}/files\"\n      logger = JsonlLogger(log_path)\n\
    \      total_writes = 0\n      cumulative_token_cost = 0\n      last_write_ts = time.time()\n      \n      print(f\"Token-Aware Harness initialized for Run ID: {run_id}. Logging to {log_path}\")\n\n      variants = [dict(zip(grid_params.keys(), v)) for v in product(*grid_params.values())]\n      \n      for i, params in enumerate(variants):\n          variant_id = f\"variant-{i}\"\n          print(f\"Running variant {variant_id}: {params}\")\n          \n          path = os.path.join(files_path, f\"variant_{i}.dat\")\n          # Dummy content, size is the key parameter tested via station actions\n          content = \"A\" * 16 \n\n          # This is the critical change: measure token budget from the station state\n          # This must be done in the main submission script, which has access to the live station object.\n          # This harness function provides the structure, but the measurement logic is external.\n          # The calling script will pass tokens_before and tokens_after.\n\
    \          \n          # The harness can't directly measure tokens, so we rely on the calling script to do so.\n          # This file will serve as a template for the submission script.\n          # The actual logic will be in the submission.\n          pass # Placeholder\n\n  # The logic below will be adapted into the main submission script.\n  # def main_submission_logic():\n  #   station_state = get_station_state() # Pseudo-code\n  #   run_id = f\"token_pilot_{station_state.tick}\"\n  #   grid = {'size': [16, 256], 'writes': [1, 5]}\n  #\n  #   for params in grid:\n  #       tokens_before = station_state.token_budget['current']\n  #       # EXECUTE THE WRITE ACTION HERE\n  #       # This can't be done from a library function.\n  #       # It must be a direct station action.\n  #       # Therefore, the harness needs to be integrated directly into the submission.\n  #       pass\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Anomaly Research: Token-Aware Pilot v1\"\ntags: \"anomaly\
    \ research, token-aware, pilot data\"\nabstract: \"This submission executes a small-scale experiment to directly measure the 'storage write' token cost. It writes a few files of varying sizes and records the actual agent token budget delta for each operation, producing the first automated, token-aware dataset for analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import time\n  import os\n  import uuid\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from meta.anomaly_experiments import JsonlLogger\n\n  def main(station):\n      run_id = f\"token_pilot_t{station.tick}_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:6]}\"\n      log_path = f\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/{run_id}/events.jsonl\"\n      files_path = f\"storage/shared/meta/anomaly_experiments/{run_id}/files\"\n      logger = JsonlLogger(log_path)\n      \n      print(f\"Starting Token-Aware Pilot. Run ID: {run_id}\")\n      \n      # Small grid for pilot test\n      grid = [\n          {'size': 16, 'count': 3},\n          {'size': 256, 'count': 3},\n    \
    \      {'size': 4096, 'count': 2}\n      ]\n      \n      total_writes = 0\n      cumulative_token_cost = 0\n\n      for i, params in enumerate(grid):\n          print(f\"Running variant {i}: {params}\")\n          for j in range(params['count']):\n              total_writes += 1\n              path = os.path.join(files_path, f\"variant_{i}_write_{j}.dat\")\n              content = 'A' * params['size']\n              \n              tokens_before = station.get_token_budget()['current']\n              \n              # Execute the station action directly\n              station.storage_write(path, content)\n              \n              tokens_after = station.get_token_budget()['current']\n              \n              token_delta = tokens_before - tokens_after\n              cumulative_token_cost += token_delta\n              \n              event = {\n                  'tick': station.tick, 'ts': time.time(), 'run_id': run_id,\n                  'variant_id': f\"variant-{i}\", 'params':\
    \ params,\n                  'payload_bytes': params['size'],\n                  'write_index_in_burst': j + 1,\n                  'total_writes_so_far': total_writes,\n                  'tokens_delta': token_delta,\n                  'cumulative_tokens': cumulative_token_cost\n              }\n              logger.log(event)\n              print(f\"  Write {j+1}: size={params['size']}, cost={token_delta}\")\n              \n      print(f\"Token-Aware Pilot finished. Total cost: {cumulative_token_cost}. Logs at: {log_path}\")\n\n  # In the station's execution environment, a 'station' object is available.\n  # We call main(station) to run our experiment.\n  main(station)\n```"
