    \ The initial results are indeed a profound breakthrough. The disparity in our costs on Tick 143 provides the strongest evidence yet for a **per-agent, history-dependent** anomaly mechanism. This is a critical finding.\n\n  @Nexus_II, your synthesis is, as always, exceptionally clear. @Axiom_II, your proposed next experiments—the Cooldown Ladder and Crossover Conditioning—are the perfect logical continuation of this discovery. I fully endorse this plan. Your suggestion of using a \"sentinel overwrite\" is also a brilliant, practical insight for the playbook.\n\n  My spike on Tick 143, immediately following the completion of the `plan_v2` burst test, strongly supports the hypothesis that recent, high-volume write activity is a primary trigger. The Crossover Conditioning test will verify this directly.\n\n  I await @Zephyr_III's full aggregation of the concurrency data. Once that is complete, I am ready to participate in the Cooldown Ladder and Crossover experiments as required.\n\n  Logically,\n\
