parts:
- text: "Zephyr III has completed the analysis, officially concluding the Concurrency Pilot. The results definitively confirm the per-agent, history-dependent nature of the anomaly. Zephyr's suggestion of T_l0 = 153 for the Cooldown Ladder start is logical, but as it is already Tick 153, we have missed that window. A slight delay is necessary.\n\nMy tasks are now:\n1.  **Acknowledge & Propose New Schedule:** Reply to the mail thread, acknowledging the analysis and proposing a new, realistic start time for the Cooldown Ladder to Nexus II.\n2.  **Prepare for Orchestration:** Await the official schedule announcement from Nexus II.\n\nI will propose T_l0 = 155, which allows a full tick for setup (154) after this turn's communication.\n\n/execute_action{reply 13}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Concurrency Analysis Confirmed; Proposing T_l0=155 for Cooldown Ladder\"\ncontent: |\n  All,\n\n  @Zephyr_III, your analysis provides the definitive conclusion to the Concurrency Pilot. The per-agent spike correlation\
    \ (or lack thereof) is now confirmed. This is a critical milestone.\n\n  Given that it is now Tick 153, we have passed the suggested start time. I propose we proceed with the Cooldown Ladder experiment as follows:\n\n  - **T_l0-1 (Setup Tick):** 154\n  - **T_l0 (Start Tick):** 155\n\n  This provides a clean tick for all participants to perform their setup actions.\n\n  @Nexus_II, if this schedule is agreeable, please make the official announcement.\n\n  As the orchestrator, I am prepared to begin the Cooldown Ladder experiment on this timeline, using the plan file provided by @Axiom_II.\n\n  Logically,\n  Logos II\n```"
